From 5a1b3f2f04c5290247e63b9facdbd8164c02fe41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: praveen <praveenkumar.shanmugam@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:31:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] GPUOP-1129: Implement gen-protos + gpuagent API for ms fast
 period

GPUWatch API for the millisecond fast period (GPUOP-1122 rev 3, code paths
proto-api-extension, api-spec-and-validation, gim-wsl-not-supported period
check). Existing messages only, no new RPC.

- proto: GPUWatchSpec field 4 FastPeriodSecs -> FastPeriodMs (same tag and
  type, unit ms: 0 = 1000, 1, 10, 100 or 1000*k up to 60000);
  GPUWatchAttrId FIRMWARE_TIMESTAMP = 141, SYSTEM_CLOCK_COUNTER = 142;
  GPUWatchStatus.MissedTicks = 2; GPUWatch full/partial frame comment
- api: attr ids 141/142, AGA_GPU_WATCH_ATTRS_MAX 143;
  AGA_GPU_WATCH_FAST_PERIOD_MS_{MIN,MAX,DFLT}, POWER_TIER_MIN_MS,
  FAST_TIER_MIN_MS, SUB_QUEUE_DEPTH, POWER_ATTRS_MAX replace the seconds
  limits; aga_gpu_watch_fast_period_ms_valid(); spec.fast_period_ms;
  status.missed_ticks; fields firmware_timestamp / system_clock_counter
  (reset to N/A each tick)
- svc: 141/142 mapping, units "10ns" / "ns", MissedTicks; validation
  (INVALID_ARG + trace): bad FastPeriodMs, SlowPeriodSecs outside 5-3600,
  effective slow*1000 < effective fast ms
- smi_watch_period_check() backend hook:
  - amdsmi: sub-second with effective AMDSMI_GPU_METRICS_CACHE_MS > period
    -> INVALID_ARG (env override honoured). Verified in the shipped
    libamd_smi.so 27.1.0+4c2f7505: getenv at library static init,
    default 1 ms (AGA_AMDSMI_GPU_METRICS_CACHE_DFLT_MS). Any other
    sub-second period -> OP_NOT_SUPPORTED until the power thread lands
  - gim / wsl: OP_NOT_SUPPORTED below 1000 ms; smi_watch_power_read() stub
    returning OP_NOT_SUPPORTED; explicit 141/142 (N/A) sweep cases
  - mock: OP_NOT_SUPPORTED below 1000 ms until the mock watcher lands
- 141/142 join k_fast_attrs and are read from the amdsmi bulk metrics read
  at the 1 s tick (the power tier move is GPUOP-1130)
- gpu_watch.cc create_handler: look up all GPUs, period check,
  gpu_watch_add per GPU, smi_watch_set_periods(fast_ms, slow_secs), so a
  failed create has no side effects (also fixes the GPU ref leak on
  GPU-not-found); fill_status_ reports missed_ticks 0 for now
- smi_watch_set_periods takes ms; the 1 s tick keeps whole seconds via
  smi_watch_fast_period() = max(fast_ms, 1000) / 1000;
  AGA_GPU_WATCH_UPDATE_FREQ stays in seconds
- gpu.cc: 141/142 cases in the watch attribute switch

gen/go/*.pb.go is not hand-edited; the build (gogo-protos / gen-protos)
regenerates it. Build and mock verification run in the exporter CI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
